# 2026-09-08 work log

What was changed and what was run, in order, one line each. Detail lives in the
commit it points to; findings go upstream as PRs. This file is the thread, not
the record.

The day's work was in `rust-codex-compiler` (hashes below are that repo) plus
outbound to `damiant3/Cobblestone`. The ladder is retired and is not touched;
it holds the log because a log belongs in a repo anyone can read.

## The self-host IR diff: 2,417 -> 2,845 of 2,846 definitions

Diffing the whole compiler's own IR against `codexir` at the same pin, per
definition. Each line is a rule read off the oracle with a probe and pinned by
a test.

    8ae473e  LinkedList is not a constructor; i64-min is a wire atom      +120
    d4acafd  `[]` infers a bare variable, so it can be a LinkedList        +61
    0ee6b00  the callee's parameter is the argument's expectation         +187
    496801d  the overflow mode is part of the operator's name               +7
    cf16816  lowering has a scope; a shadowing binder is re-spelled        +25
    ed58ae8  the pipeline runs BEFORE the lift -- 0 definitions missing    +10
    42bfd74  RESOLVE is a phase; a Text sorts in CCE order, not ASCII      +18
    b0a0788  a let's bindings do not outlive their definition               +3
    8b3377b  a let statement swallows its act block; generic fields        +2
    260b8fa  a field store meets the field type and answers the record      +1
    be8841e  __record-set names its field with a text literal               +2
    94ceaaa  the two arms of an if meet; the condition meets Boolean        +1
    99a4824  arithmetic answers the tighter type                            +1

The one definition still differing is upstream's, filed as PR 134.

## The corpus: 19 crashes to 0

    7aa1f50  an occurs check, and `linear` is transparent to unification

Found by sweeping all 1,246 units rather than by a gate -- `irdump gradewhole`
aborted partway and the abort was the interesting part. 1,190 -> 1,208 lower,
38 refuse with a reason, 0 crash.

## Gate repair

    d107814  safari/run.sh reads safari's arm-gaps.tsv instead of a copy

`treesspec` had been reported WRONG for three days while the answer sat in
`spec/arm-gaps.tsv` one repo over. Not a regression; issue 125's third
instance. Confirmed independently: Cobblestone reads `11.700000000000001` as
bits ...750 where correctly-rounded is ...751.

